comments.body:
@vwbaker  can we send a PR that just removes the normalization from the test? I also don't understand why we would be post-processing the results, rather than just comparing them as they are.

Post-processing just has the potential to hide issues, as you're mentioning.

It's also a 3rd separate issue discussed in this thread, so I would like to have a separate discussion contained to that one, since clearly conveying all the interdependencies is becoming a bit difficult here 😄

